message: "Please cite this research preprint as follows."
title: "Beyond the Biological Bottleneck: Could Intelligence Emerge Directly from Nature?"
subtitle: "A Framework for Natural Computation, Abiotic Agency, and Distinguishing Emergence from Construction"
authors:
  - family-names: Debnath
    given-names: Devanik
    affiliation: Independent Research
    website: https://github.com/Devanik21
date-released: "2026-10-30"
notes: "AI assistance is disclosed in the manuscript; the named human author is responsible for the final work."
type: article
license: CC-BY-4.0
repository-code: https://github.com/Devanik21/The-Invention-Archive
abstract: >-
  This preprint examines whether biological evolution is a necessary intermediate
  in the emergence of intelligence. It separates physical computation, adaptive
  capability, minimal agency, and functional intelligence from causal origin,
  and formalizes a non-identifiability result: when functional observation
  likelihoods coincide under direct abiotic emergence and constructed-origin
  hypotheses, functional behaviour alone cannot distinguish those histories.
keywords:
  - astrobiology
  - abiotic computation
  - physical reservoir computing
  - agency
  - planetary intelligence
  - technosignatures
  - information thermodynamics
  - Bayesian identifiability
